/* Presentation-only 19 October 2026 results layer. */
(()=>{const q=s=>document.querySelector(s), mk=(t,h)=>{const e=document.createElement(t);e.innerHTML=h;return e}, link=n=>`<a href="evening-20261019/${n}" download>Download data</a>`;
const origin='<p class="origin-line">Origin: New analysis · 19 October 2026</p>', how=x=>`<div class="how-to-read"><strong>How to read this figure.</strong> ${x}</div>`;
const t=`<table><thead><tr><th>t-SNE setting</th><th>Noise included</th><th>Assigned only</th></tr></thead><tbody>${[['Euclidean · 0.005','+0.015 [−0.053, +0.084]; 58%','+0.041 [−0.035, +0.117]; 51%'],['Euclidean · 0.01','+0.003 [−0.058, +0.065]; 56%','−0.005 [−0.076, +0.059]; 60%'],['Euclidean · 0.02','+0.031 [−0.015, +0.076]; 58%','+0.058 [−0.017, +0.126]; 65%'],['Cosine · 0.005','−0.006 [−0.084, +0.078]; 47%','+0.027 [−0.072, +0.127]; 53%'],['Cosine · 0.01','−0.004 [−0.077, +0.070]; 44%','−0.038 [−0.126, +0.057]; 40%'],['Cosine · 0.02','−0.029 [−0.092, +0.038]; 37%','+0.019 [−0.062, +0.112]; 47%']].map(r=>'<tr>'+r.map(x=>'<td>'+x+'</td>').join('')+'</tr>').join('')}</tbody></table>`;
const block=mk('section',`<div class="evening-results"><h2 id="evening-results">Validated results and run ledger · 19 October 2026</h2>${origin}<p>New results are a <strong>GPU-native numeric-LR t-SNE sensitivity</strong>; historical scikit-learn schedule equivalence is not claimed. Historical results remain separate.</p><details open><summary>LR=200 t-SNE: tutor versus equal-weight mean pupil (43 families)</summary><p>Mean pupil H minus tutor H (bits), family bootstrap 95% interval; share above zero.</p>${t}<p><em>All twelve intervals contain 0: no detectable difference, not no difference. Descriptive only; families are not independent and no p-values are shown.</em> ${link('lr200_tsne_results.json')}</p>${how('Settings: random initialisation, FFT, perplexity 30, 1,000 iterations, adaptive schedule; effective learning rate max(N/3,1), so nominal 200 is ignored by this cuML mode. The historical explorer remains the 13 October snapshot.')}</details><details><summary>Small-sample check of entropy</summary>${origin}<p>Plug-in H underestimates entropy at small n; Miller–Madow adds (K−1)/(2n ln 2) bits. Median correction: 0.006 bits across 4,932 bird rows; 0.063 for 153 rows with n&lt;200 (maximum 0.165). Over 797 partitions, pupil−tutor gaps were −0.063/−0.064 plug-in, −0.060/−0.060 Miller–Madow, and −0.051/−0.051 rarefied (inclusive/assigned). The no-detectable-difference result does not depend on estimator. ${link('bias_per_bird.csv')} · ${link('bias_family_gaps.csv')}</p>${how('A correction near zero means sample-size bias is small; this is an estimator check, not evidence of biological equivalence.')}</details><details><summary>Category overlap between tutor and pupils</summary>${origin}<p>Equal entropy does not mean shared categories. For 1,669 pairs/treatment: inclusive median JSD 0.616 bits vs 0.004 null, overlap 0.258, 100.0% above null; assigned-only 0.696 vs 0.005, overlap 0.191, 99.9%. Joint family fitting means low overlap may reflect session or individual clusters, not copying accuracy. ${link('tutor_pupil_overlap.csv')}</p>${how('JSD compares distributions; overlap is Σmin(p,q). Both are descriptive family-local quantities, not cross-family homology.')}</details><details><summary>Calibration of the Hopkins statistic</summary>${origin}<p>At N=10,000, mean H: square 0.501; L-shape 0.017; ring 0.0071; one smooth Gaussian blob 0.061; three blobs 0.0017. Thus very small H alone does not prove clusters: 0.5 occurs only when data fill their convex hull. <strong>Open item*:</strong> apply this calibration to observed embeddings. ${link('hopkins_null_calibration.csv')}</p>${how('The simulations use the same implementation, convex-hull null, squared 2-D distances, 10% sampling and 500 repeats per cell.')}</details><details><summary>Complete family and tutor-group coverage</summary>${origin}<p><strong>166 birds</strong>: 406,625 source intervals; 1,793 rejected; 404,832 retained; 785 retained below 5 ms (unreviewed); 0 retained-versus-analysed consistency issues. ${link('counts_per_bird.csv')}</p></details><details><summary>Provenance of the S2 inputs</summary>${origin}<p>The S2 CSV has 1,692 tutor rows: 1,594 match the published snapshot with 0 value mismatches. The other 98 rows (49 partitions) have matching entropy: 96 from large-family results and 2 from family_batch_009; Y_875 PCoA-cosine 0.02 is among them. S7 numbers are unchanged. ${link('provenance_s2_rows_not_in_published_snapshot.csv')}</p></details><details open><summary>Run ledger and open tasks · 19 October 2026</summary>${origin}<p><strong>Completed:</strong> 43 families × 6 partitions = 258 LR=200 t-SNE partitions; primary (7 plus adopted LB12), secondary (19), evening A (15), evening B (LG281). CPU provenance, counts, bias, overlap and Hopkins calibration completed; counts ran after GPU lanes to avoid HDD saturation. S1–S3 validations completed 18 October.</p><p><strong>Open tasks*:</strong> HP10, LG181, Aq12 CUDA OOM; Aq33 host-RAM guard; Gry12/Y875 too large; DB3, Aq2, Aq4, LB13, Wh10, DG1, Y2/Y875 incomplete catalogued families; R39/Y16 unresolved audio; frozen S7 22-lineage cohort not computed; pair queue 113 pending, 1 failed, 1 held; 48 PCA and 18 PHATE/UMAP resource blocks; privacy review; 5-ms review; Hopkins-to-observed calibration; tutor–pupil regression; cross-family homology. * excluded for now; see Exclusions and asterisks. ${link('lr200_run_ledger.json')} · ${link('evening_run_summary.json')} · ${link('MANIFEST.sha256')}</p></details></div>`);
const anchor=q('#interactive-visualizations'); if(anchor) anchor.before(block); const toc=q('.sidebox'); if(toc) toc.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend','<a href="#evening-results">19 Oct results & run ledger</a>');
const style=mk('style','.evening-results{padding:1.2rem;margin:1rem 0;border:1px solid #b9ced0;border-radius:12px;background:#fbfdfd}.evening-results table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.9rem}.evening-results th,.evening-results td{padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid #d8e2e4;text-align:left}.evening-results details{margin:.7rem 0}.how-to-read{margin:.7rem 0;padding:.7rem;border-left:4px solid #087f79;background:#eff8f6}.evening-results a{font-weight:600}');document.head.append(style);
})();
